[ceiling] The eight aft zip-tie routing channels — each flat is the roof of a 3.5 mm-high channel open through the carrier's aft face. Extrusion strands bridge only the web's 2.5 mm Y thickness, while the 18.5 mm X run lies along those strands; the square roof preserves a flush 2.5 mm tie path and traps no support.
